# Copy to .env at the repo root and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit it.
#
# The HOST pi agent's own registry (~/.pi/agent/auth.json + models-store.json)
# remains the PRIMARY credential path: `just sbx lifecycle fill` mirrors that
# registry into every sandbox. The LLM API keys below are an OPTIONAL second path
# for tools that read keys from the environment. See README.md -> Install.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM API keys (optional) — provisioned INTO every sandbox by FILL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Any of these you set here are copied to app/.env (0600) on each sandbox by
# `just sbx lifecycle fill`. Only the names on this allowlist ever cross;
# single-line values only. Remember: a sandbox is disposable but not private —
# prefer per-provider keys you are comfortable seeing on a throwaway VM, and
# rotate any key you suspect leaked. The pi registry mirror (host
# ~/.pi/agent) stays the primary credential path and needs nothing here.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# ZAI_API_KEY=
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# KIMI_API_KEY=
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional overrides
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary if not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# SSSF_CONFIG=adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml
